      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-06-28_WidnesExaminer_art0028" n="art0028">
        <head>What are you koking for?</head>
        <p>What are you koking for?</p>
        <p>"I am looking for a recipe—l feel sure it was • put safely in this drawer, but now there's no sign of it." "O 1 what was it?"</p>
        <p>"A 'recipe I cut out of a news/paper, I know it's a splendid one because I've tried it already." "Ah! here it is at last—just listen 'how easy."..</p>
        <p>To make CRYSTAL PUDDING. Take a pint packet of BIRD'S Crystal Jelly Powder (Lemon Flavor) ; 1 Sponge Cake; 1 Stewed Apple; ,a few glace or crystalised Cherries. Make the Jelly according to the directions; cut cherries in half and decorate the bottotn'of a mould with them; pour in a little of the jelly just covering the cherries and allow to set. Then cut the sponge cake in four slices and spread with the stewed apple. When the jelly in the mould is set, add to it carefully the rest of the jelly which must be nearly cold. Place the sponge cake in the middle, and when the whole is set firm turn out in the ordinary. way. • BIRD'S CRYSTAL JELLY POWDERS are sold in many varieties br all Grocers in 2d., .314. and 6cl. packets. J-101</p>
