        <p>Poole—Cunningham. A marriag3, which aroused considerable local interest, was solemnised at Runcorn Parish Church, Wednesday. The contracting parties- were Miss Dorothy Cunningham, only daughter of Mr. and Mrs. W. J. Cunningham, of Norman-road, Runcorn, and the Rev. N.J. Poole, vicar of St. James's, Hull, and formerly curate at Holy Trinity Church, Runcorn, and St. Paul's Church, Widnes. The bride was actired in white satin, trimmed with ninon, and wore a white pictui e hat, and carried a bouquet of roses and lilies. The ceremony was performed by the Rev. S. J. Poole, brother of the bridegroom, of St. James's, Church, Gravesend, and the Rev. Douglas M. Moreton, vicar of St. 'Thomas's Wavertree. The best man was Mr. Bruce Cunningham, brother of tile bride. A large number of costly presents were received, includ- ing a solid silver teapot from the Mill Brow Mission, where the bride and her father had taken an active and useful interest. The bride was given away by her father. The honeymoon is being spent in the Lake district.</p>
