        <p>Where Social Reform Fails. ,s.rok tl'ing at Bold-street Wesleyan Church on Sunday, 4tv. /1118 text" The unsearchable riches of Christ," the htion ' Williamson pointed out the true remedy for the social ills with which the people of this age sfor„.leted. This was undoubtedly an age when Social was the popular aim. But the people who were °l,e to redress our social anomalies needed to tatorta what it was they hoped to confer on the r°444:'ates, and whom they really helped by their towards Social Reform. For the mcst part the O'er° of a material character, and were not of ,ißber the soul of man. The modern demands for 14414 wages and better housing were really estimable tpqd r'd Perfectly just. But when summed up they lttle, save physical comfort and material wealth. taft terfat weakness was found in the fact that they '5 lite spiritual side entirely untouched,doing nothing t..he inner wealth and to confer the freedom Il'ltlea`which man's in Christ Jens. Moreover, often- toilehua People who really stood in need of help were ad by the present methods of Social Reform. „tllss of 'life were not always logical and the poorest w:_o not necessarily to be found among the low- _</p>
