      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-06-28_WidnesExaminer_art0162" n="art0162">
        <head>Examiner, Saturday, June 28, 1913. STOCKTON 111 EATH.</head>
        <p>The Examiner, Saturday, June 28, 1913. STOCKTON 111 EATH.</p>
        <p>COUNCIL SCHOOL MANAGERS.—The first meeting cf</p>
        <p>the newly-elected managers of the Council school-was held on Tuesday evening. The following are the managers :—Messrs. T. Baxter, G. Pilling, H. J. West- brook, J. J. Whitley, Roger C. Parr, J. Cooper, J. Nixon, and W. Mclntyre (representing the administrative education authority),, F. Pearson and J. M cDermid (representing Stockton Heath).W. H. Woodcock (Lower Walton), and W. Roberts (Latchford Without), the parishes named being the contributory area served by the school. Mr. Piling was re-elected chairman, and Mr. Westbrook vice-chairman.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-06-28_WidnesExaminer_art0163" n="art0163">
        <head>PENKETH.</head>
        <p>PENKETH.</p>
        <p>CHILD KNOCKED DOWN BY MOTOR CAR.—On Wed- nesday afternoon, as the children were returning home from school, the daughter of Mr. J. Fisher was knocked down by a motor car, hailing from Warrington. Fortunately, the car was travelling very slowly, and the girl was not seriously injured. The occupants showed every kindness towards her. FREE TRADE I.l7.ctoK.—An open-air meeting was held (in connection with the above Crnion, on Wednesday evening, on the recreation ground, Penketh. Mr. M. Nicolson, of Liverpool, was the speaker, and gave an iateresting address. Mr. F. Gill presided.</p>
        <p>_ Dressmaking (Intermediate).—First class : Daisy , Andrews, Alice Fairhurst, Margaret Tabernacle. Second class: Lily Crawshaw, Alice Foden, Ada Phillips. Pass: Annie H. Bell, Amy Bleasdale, Clara Bowden, Rosa Hodson, Elizabeth Holmes, Ella Morley, Nellie Simister, Agnes Vernon, Elsie Webb, Fanny Wilkinson, Annie Williams. Dressmaking (Elementary.)—First class: Margaret Garner, Gertrude Jones, Rose Lawton, Amy Lowe, Gladys Podmore, Marion Simpson, Elizabeth VVillcock, Nellie William. Second alas : Evelyn Booth, Gladys Cotterill, Amy Cragg, Anna Davies, Mabel Dutton, Anne Hayes, Laurette Hayes, May Higher°, May Hill, Gladys E. Ice, Alice V. Lowe, Doris Merrill, Gladys Pomfret, Margaret Reynolds, Lily Shaw, Sarah Shuttle worth, Kate Spencer, Bessie Warburton, Alice Wood. Pass : Lucy Ashurst, Ellen Bond, Veronica Brady, Elizabeth Brooks, Clara Brown, Sarah Brown, Catherine Callaghan, Annie Chile, Mary Dillon, Nellie Gamble, Doris Garnett, Sarsh Gregory. Eva Hankinson, Annie Hitclimough, Amy Holt, May Holt, Bessie Jolley, Mary Kelly, Doris Kinsey, Elsie Leigh, Nellie McCormack, Mary MoGeer, Edith Mitchell, Elsie Morris, Ida Peake, Florence Roberts, Leah Rowe, Gladys Starkie, Eva A. Tanner, Ada Wallington, Mary Weston, Edith Yates. Millinery (Advanced).—First class: Annie Ball, Edith Blomeley, Priscilla Cotterill, Lillie Crawshaw, Alice Foden Gladys King. Second class: Ada Armitage, Gladys Backhouse, Gladys Belshavr, Clara Bowden, Olive M. Dale, Alice Fairhurst, Minnie Harrill), Amy Kirkham, Edna Rowe, Nellie Simister, Daisy Smallwood, Bessie Speakman, Annie Taylor, Florence V. Tort, Agnes Vernon, Ethel Whitby, Annie Williams, Ethel Wood, Annie Wright, Edith Yarwood. Pass: Amy Bleasdale, Emily Gibbs, Elizabeth Holmes, Ella M. Morley, Ada Paillips, Gladys Poole, Dora Small- wood, Lilian Smith, Margaret Tabernacle, Annie Webb, Elsie Webb, Fanny Wilkinson. Millinery (Elementary).—First class: Elizabeth Brooks, Clara Brown, Margaret Garner, Doris Garnett, Laurette Hayes, Amy Hon, May Holt, May Jefferson, Gertrude Jones, Doris Kinsey, Amy Lowe, Marion Simpson, Eva Tanner, Elizabeth Willcock. Second class: Lucy Ashurst, Ellen Bond, Evelyn Booth, Veronica Brady, Sarah Brown, Ellen Burrows, Annie Cliffe, Gladys Cotteril, Amy Crags, Anna Davies, Mary Dillon, Ellen Dobson, Ellen Gordon, Sarah Gregory, Eva Hankinson, Annie Hayes, May Hill, Gladys E. Ince,_ Florence Jackson, Bessie Jolley, Mary Kelley, Rose Lawton, Elsie Leigh, Alice V. Lowe, Edith Mitchell, Ellen Monks, Elsie Morris, Laura Murray, Gladys Podmore, Gladys Pomfret, Florence V. Roberts, Leah Rowe, Kate Spencer, Lily Sudlow, Ellen Ada Wallington Bessie Warburton, Ethel Whittaker, Lily Willcock, Nellie Williams, Nellie Williamson, Alice Wood, Edith Yates. Pass: Lily Ashurst, Hannah Booth, Mabel Dutton, Nellie Gamble, Annie W. Hardy, May Higham, Annie Hirchmeugh, Nellie M..:Cormack, Mary McGeer, Doris Merrill, Ida Peaks, Margaret Reynolds, Sarah Shuttleworth, Gladys Starkie, Harriet A. Thomas, Mary J. Weston. Needlework (Advanced).—First class: Anna Davies, Mary Kelly, Ellen Shuttleworth. Second class: Annie Cliffe, Gladys Cotterill, Sarah Gregory, Lauretta Hayes, May Highans; Doris Merrill, Ida Peake, Marion Simpson, Eva Tanner, Harriet A. Thomas, Nellie Williams, Nellie Williamson. Pass : Evelyn Booth, Sarah Brown, Mary Dillon, May Hill, Bessie Jolley, Elsie Morris, Laura Murray, Ellen Twilit], Bessie Warburton. ' Elements of Home Nursing.—First class: Ada Armitage, Amy Kirkham. Second class: Agnes Bannon, Mabel Crane, Rosa M. Hodson, Ethel Whitby. Pass: Gladys Backhouse, Minnie Harrop, Maggie Toft, Annie Williams, Edith Yarwood. Practical Drawing (Building).—Distinction : Ralph Acton, Thomas Evans (let place in Lancashire and ' Cheshire), Stanley Jerams (2nd place in Lancashire and Cheshire), Frank Lee, Arthur Se intors First class: Frederic Gee, Samuel Hankioson, John Hensbaw, John ' Lea, James Massey, George E. Owen,Thomas Warburton. Second class: Stanley C. Appleton