      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-06-28_WidnesExaminer_art0214" n="art0214">
        <head>TO-DAY'S FINAL.</head>
        <p>TO-DAY'S FINAL.</p>
        <p>Mr. A. H. Crosfield to Present the Cup and Watches.</p>
        <p>The "Peter Peacock" Challenge Cup competition. which reaches its final stage to-day, has proved more popular than ever this season. On the whole the weather has been kind has been kind to the bowling fraternity, and the quality of the games has been of a high character. Mr. Campbell has kept Bank Quay green in fine condition, and everything has been done by the officials of the Association to make the Saturday afternoons of members as enjoyable as possible. The games to-day will be :</p>
        <p>FOURTH ROUND.</p>
        <p>1. 2.0. St. Austin's ov. St. John's B. 2. 2.45 Whitecross F v Orford A. 3. 3.30 Town Hall D v. St. Austin's F. 4. 4.15 St. Austin's Dor Fairfield G. SEMI-FINAL.</p>
        <p>5.0. Winner of No. 1 v Winner of No. 2. 5.45. Winner of No. 3v. Winner of No. 4. FINAL AT 7 O'CLOCK._</p>
        <p>—.„— Referee, R. H. Halford ; measurers, S. H. Walker and E. J. Davies; gatekeepers, J. Bailey and W. Vose. Mr. A. H. Crosfield, who shows a keen interest in all kinds of sport, has promised to present the cup and watches to the successful team. A large attend- ance is expected, and everything will be done to ensure the comfort of visitors.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1913-06-28_WidnesExaminer_art0215" n="art0215">
        <head>"HAROLD SMITH" CHALLENGE CUP.</head>
        <p>"HAROLD SMITH" CHALLENGE CUP.</p>
        <p>The second round of this competition was concluded on the Brooklands Hotel Green on Saturday, the results being : St. Austin's No. 3. Bewsey N 0.3.. W Forster (capt.) 5 T Taylor ... 35 T Cheaters ... 13 J Pritchard (capt.) ... 15</p>
