        <p>TO BUILDERS AND CONTRACTORS.— ESTIMATES are required for a small alteration to the Orford-lane Confectionery Department of the Warrington E.I. Co-operative Society, Ltd. The successful Contractor will be required to enter into an undertaking to pay all workmen employed on or in connection with the work the standard rates of wages in force in the district. The Committee do not bind themselves to accept the lowest nor any tender. Application for particulars to be made on or before July 3rd next to ALBERT WARBURTON, A.R.1.8.A., Architect, 2, Bold-street, Warrington.</p>
        <p>00UNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.— The SANITARY WORKS COMMITTEE invite TENDERS for the SUPPLY of 20 TONS of CLEAN BATTEN WHEAT STRAW, to be delivered at Howley Central Sanitary Depot, in 5 or 10 ton lots or as the Committee may direct. Tenders to be sent in securely fastened envelopes endorsed "Tenders for Straw," and addreesod "The Chairman, Sanitary Works Committee, Town Hall, Warrington," not later than Tuesday, July Bth, 1913, Samples to be sent with Tender. The Committee reserve to themselves the right to accept or reject the whole or part of any Tender. JAMES J. A. PARFITT, Cleansing Superintendent. Cleansing Department, June 250, 1913</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON.—The SANITARY WORKS COMMITTEE are pre- pared to receive TENDERS for the supply of a MILD STEEL SHAKE', 71in. square and 17ft. Bin. long, to be delivered free at Longford Depot. Further particulars may be obtained from the undersigned. The contractor whose tender is accepted will be requireu to observe the recognised customs and conditio.,A as to rate of wages and working hours prevailing within the district. Tenders, securely fastened, must be addressed "The Chairman, Sanitary IVorks Committee, Town Hall, Warrington," endorsed "Tender for Steel Shaft," and delivered not later than Saturday, July 12th, 1913. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. Longford Depot, R. WILSON, Warrington, June 25th, 1913. Manager.</p>
        <p>COUNTY BOROUGH OF WARRINGTON ELECTRICITY DEPARTMENT. The ELECTRICITY and TRAMWAYS COMMITTEE INVITE TENDERS for the SUPPLY of 10,000 Tons of SLACK to be delivered at the Electricity Works, Howley, during 12 months commencing let August next, to be delivered in accordance with conditions of Specification, copy of which can be obtained from the undersigned on payment of One Guinea, which will he returned on receipt of a bona-fide tender. Five shillings will be charged for extra copies of specifica- tion. In the altornative the Committee invite Tenders for 5,000 tons of SLACK for delivery during the six months commencing Ist August next. The above quantities may at the option of the Engineer be increased during breakdown or other emergency by 10 per cent. above the average supply per day. Tenders, addressed to the "Chairman of the Electricity and Tramways Committee, Town Hall, War- rington," must be sealed with wax and endorsed "'Tender for Slack," and delivered not later than 12 o'clock noon on Tuesday, July Bth, 1913. The lowest or any tender will not necessarily be accepted. F. V. L. MATHIAS. ' Borough Electrical and Howley, Warrington. Tramways Engineer.</p>
